The most direct and robust fix for an "undeclared" Kconfig symbol within a Zephyr core header, when the Kconfig system fails to provide it, is to add a fallback definition directly in the header file. This ensures that the symbol is always defined, preventing the compilation error. A common default stack size for Zephyr threads is 1024 bytes.

